We need to express: if the deque originally contained the element (i.e., before removal, contains(o) true), then the method returns true. The method returns boolean result (the return value). So assert: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result.

But also maybe need to consider that if not originally contained, result may be false. But comment only says "If the deque originally contained the element, then the result of the removal is true." So we assert implication: old contains => result.

Thus final code: <code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result;</code>

